"[2505.11457] Noise sensitivity of crossings for high temperature Ising model (https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.11457)\nciteturn2view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.11457\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Probability\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 16 May 2025 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 6 Aug 2025 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Noise sensitivity of crossings for high temperature Ising model\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Vincent Tassion , cite7†Hugo Vanneuville L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Noise sensitivity of crossings for high temperature Ising model, by Vincent Tassion and Hugo Vanneuville\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Consider the event that there is a $+$ crossing from left to right in a box for the Ising model on the triangular lattice. We show that this event is noise sensitive under Glauber dynamics $t \\mapsto \\sigma_t$ in the subcritical regime $\\beta<\\beta_c$. We rely on the non-spectral approach from our previous work [TV23].\nL17: An important aspect in this more general setup is the study of the pair $(\\sigma_0,\\sigma_t)$ and in particular the establishment of properties such as finite-energy and spatial mixing.\nL18: Comments:  | 44 pages, minor changes introduced\nL19: Subjects:  | Probability (math.PR); Mathematical Physics (math-ph)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2505.11457 [math.PR]\nL21:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2505.11457v2 [math.PR] for this version)\nL22:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2505.11457†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Hugo Vanneuville [cite13†view email ]